      "content": "I see your point about the language style. But I'm wondering if you think the actual content matters as much here? If you look closely at Dr. Adeyemi's research, he's dealing with localized field data which is incredibly complex, whereas Sterling is doing more high-level modeling. Do you think there's a risk that \"academic\" sounding language is just masking a lack of depth, or does the way it's written fundamentally change how much we should trust the scientific validity of the findings in these two cases?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
